</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKI RYUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAHI GLASS COMPANY, LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUNAKI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKI, RYUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUNAKI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKI RYUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUNAKI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKI, RYUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A water-and-oil repellant composition of the aqueous dispersion type which changes little in viscosity upon repetitions of freezing/thawing and has excellent storage stability.  In particular, the water-and-oil repellant composition can stably impart to paper excellent resistance to water and oils. The composition contains a polyfluoroalkyl-containing phosphoric acid salt in combination with a compound miscible with water in any proportion and having a flash point of 50 to 150 DEG C (propylene glycol, etc.).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition hydrophobe et oléophobe de type dispersion aqueuse dont la viscosité varie peu après des opérations répétées de congélation/décongélation et dont la stabilité de stockage est excellente. L'invention concerne plus particulièrement une composition hydrophobe et oléophobe susceptible de conférer au papier une forte résistance à l'eau et à l'huile. La composition comprend un sel d'acide phosphorique contenant un polyfluoralkyle combiné à un composé hydromiscible selon une proportion quelconque et dont le point d'éclair oscille entre 50 et 150  DEG C (propylène glycol, etc.).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>